BT 1 0 0 1 0 74 Tm /F1 10 Tf 12 TL .201894 Tw (Some series of NXP G2X tags \(such as G2iM and G2iM+\) support the ChangeConfig command, which can be used) Tj T* 0 Tw .529719 Tw (to read or modify the 16bits Config-Word of NXP G2X tags. The Config-Word of the NXP G2X tag is located at the) Tj T* 0 Tw .133528 Tw (address 20h \(word address\) of EPC Memory Bank and can be read by a normal Read command. When the tag is in) Tj T* 0 Tw 2.345783 Tw (the Secured state \(safe state\), the Config-Word of the tag can be rewritten. It should be noted that rewriting) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.044006 Tw (Config-Word means flipping the corresponding data bit of Config-Word, that is, writing the corresponding bit of \2211\222) Tj T* 0 Tw 2.295256 Tw (flipping \(\2211 \221Becomes \2210\222, \2210\222 becomes \2211\222\), the corresponding bit written in \2210\222 remains unchanged. Before this) Tj T* 0 Tw (instruction, the Select parameter should be set to select the specified label for operation.) Tj T* ET
